{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EVIDENCE for 'Each deletion is a separate commit so either can be reverted independently'.\n\nThe two deletions landed on origin/main as two distinct commits, pushed as two distinct Gerrit changes (a relation chain), so either can be reverted on its own:\n\n  6d8ea3143a  Delete dead bug_close_reason_ok predicate      (Gerrit change 1475)\n  c89a2ddcc4  Delete the dead reconciler _attestation module (Gerrit change 1476)\n\nCommand and output:\n  $ git log origin/main --oneline --grep=723f -5\n  c89a2ddcc4 Delete the dead reconciler _attestation module\n  6d8ea3143a Delete dead bug_close_reason_ok predicate\n\nBoth carry the rebar-ticket: 723f-c5b2-d83b-43cb trailer and a DCO sign-off, and both are Verified +1 / LLM-Review +1 and MERGED. The criterion is met on main; it is not visible from a worktree HEAD that predates the merge, which is why the verifier could not see it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786096984457781001,"uuid":"e8fdaa8d-e15a-400b-b5af-e3811a516646"}